{{!< default}}
{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  home.hbs — the front page.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: routes.yaml maps `/` to this template —

      routes:
        /: home

  — and Ghost returns a 400 "Missing template home.hbs for route /" if it is
  absent. index.hbs does NOT cover it: `/` is a routed template, not the
  collection index. Deleting this file breaks the front page and nothing else,
  which makes it an easy one to miss. See abstract/decisions/0003.

  ── THE PAGE-OR-SITE FORK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  A Ghost PAGE with the slug `home` supplies the headline and lede if one
  exists; otherwise the site's own title and description do. That fork is the
  pattern every content-less route in routes.yaml uses, and it is what lets
  the front page be edited in Ghost Admin instead of here.

  ── WHAT IT IS AND IS NOT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Built from NSDS bands: a hero, then the latest posts, then a subscribe CTA.
  Everything visual comes from .ns-* classes; this file contributes no styling
  and no new class names.

  It is deliberately NOT the full home page abstract/11 and abstract/12
  describe — the training path entry points, the featured course, the weekly
  rhythm. Those need the tag vocabulary in abstract/18 settled and real
  content to read, and inventing them here would mean building the layout
  twice. What is here is correct and plain rather than speculative.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

<section class="ns-band">
  <div class="ns-band__inner">
    {{#page}}
      <p class="ns-kicker">{{t "Namaste Salesforce"}}</p>
      <h1 class="ns-hero__title">{{title}}</h1>
      {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-hero__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}

      {{!-- A `home` page's body is a real editing surface: whatever an author
            puts in it renders here, so the front page can grow sections
            without a theme change. --}}
      {{#if html}}
        <div class="gh-content ns-prose">{{content}}</div>
      {{/if}}
    {{else}}
      <p class="ns-kicker">{{t "Namaste Salesforce"}}</p>
      <h1 class="ns-hero__title">{{@site.title}}</h1>
      {{#if @site.description}}<p class="ns-hero__lede">{{@site.description}}</p>{{/if}}
    {{/page}}

    {{#if @site.members_enabled}}
      <div class="ns-hero__actions">
        {{> "chrome/members"}}
      </div>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── Latest ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  `{{#get}}` rather than the `posts` context, because `/` is a routed template
  and has no collection of its own.

  ⚠ limit="all" IS NOT SUPPORTED in {{#get}} — it silently returns 15. Use a
  real number. See CLAUDE.md.
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
{{#get "posts" limit="6" include="authors,tags" as |latest|}}
  <section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">

      <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
        <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Latest"}}</h2>
        <div class="ns-band__actions">
          <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--quiet ns-btn--sm" href="{{@site.url}}/blog/">
            {{t "All posts"}} <i class="ph ph-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      {{#if latest}}
        <div class="ns-grid">
          {{#foreach latest}}{{> "cards/blog-card"}}{{/foreach}}
        </div>
      {{else}}
        {{!-- A brand-new site with no posts is the first thing anyone sees.
              A blank band reads as a broken theme. --}}
        <p class="ns-empty">{{t "No posts yet."}}</p>
      {{/if}}

    </div>
  </section>
{{/get}}
